6. YOUR DATA AND THIRD-PARTY SERVICES
   (a) The Software runs on Your computer and stores Your data there. The
       Licensor does not receive Your accounts, chats, files or API keys.
   (b) You may connect the Software to third-party services, such as AI model
       providers, using credentials You supply. Your use of those services is
       governed by their terms, and You are responsible for any fees they
       charge and for the content You send to them.
   (c) Network connections the Software makes on its own:
       (i)   Announcements. While online, it fetches a public announcement
             file hosted on GitHub (at most about every 15 minutes, when the
             app is used) to show announcements from the Licensor, which may
             include promotional content, and update notices. The request
             carries no account data, cookies or identifiers, but like any
             internet request it reveals Your IP address to GitHub. An
             announcement with an image or video is loaded by Your browser
             from the host it names (for example YouTube). Announcements
             are part of the Software and cannot be switched off (see 3(f)).
       (ii)  AI providers and other services You connect, as described in
             (b), when You use them. To show whether a key works, the
             Software also asks each configured provider for its list of
             models; that request carries no content of Yours.
       The Software's own pages, scripts and fonts are included in it and
       are not loaded from the internet.
   (d) You are responsible for backing up Your data.

